    "text": "It is therefore clear that, when the wheel m has made a complete turn, the cart has measured a mile of space at a time, and the wheel f has only moved the space of one of its teeth, and the wheel n has done the same, which shows with its rocket each mile, just as the hand of a clock shows its hours. But the wheel f, instead of showing, makes the ear hear the noise or sound made by a small stone dropped into a vessel suitable for receiving sound."
