    "text": "For, if it were heavy, acknowledging that, from the earth upwards, with each degree of altitude, degrees of lightness are acquired, since water is lighter than earth, and air than water, and fire than air, and so on, it would seem that, if the moon had density like the moon, it would have gravity, and, having gravity, (which (I mean) that the space where it is located could not support it, and consequently it would have to descend (and join) towards the center of the universe, and join with the earth, and, if not the earth, at least its waters would have to fall and strip it of itself, and fall (at c) towards the center and leave the moon stripped of itself and without lustre; therefore, not following what reason promises us about it, it is a clear sign that this moon is clothed with its elements, that is, water, air and fire, and thus by itself supports itself in that space, as our earth does with its elements in this other space, and that heavy things perform the same function in their elements, as other heavy things do in our elements."
