    "text": "All the instruments they make often fail to function perfectly, simply because they try to fit a line so long as a limb cannot fit. It's like putting 8 into 7, which is impossible. And this is why the master composers of these instruments often remain astonished and confused, seemingly enchanted by their works, wherever some movement occurs, especially those that pass through grooves or channels."
